RESULT
  Step 1  Register IGMPv1 group report ......... PASS   group learned on DUT, querier v1
  Step 2  Traffic forwarded, no loss ........... PASS   60/60 rx, 0% loss @ 1 pps
  Step 3  "Send IGMP leave" .................... N/A    IGMPv1 has NO leave message;
                                                        membership is removed by querier
                                                        group-timeout (shown below).
  DUT is the IGMP querier; membership created by a real IGMPv1 report (type 0x12).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BENCH / TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DUT / querier : u4  S/N 264A23052  MAC 84e3.2787.09c0   (IGMP snooping querier, L3 IGMP)
  Source        : u5  S/N 264A23066  MAC 84e3.2787.0740
  Receiver/host : tb470 eth2 10.10.10.20/27  ->  u4 port1.0.2 (vlan10 access)
  Fabric        : one vlan10 (10.10.10.0/27) trunk  u4 port1.0.24 <-> u5 port2.0.24.
                  The 2nd u4<->u5 link (port*.0.26) is held shutdown so vlan10 is loop-free.

METHOD / SCOPE
  No IXIA on this bench. RECEIVER = tb470 host sending a REAL IGMPv1 membership report
  (scapy, src 10.10.10.20 to pass the DUT source-address check) and counting frames with
  tcpdump; SOURCE = u5 `ping <group>` at 1 pps. Functional test, NOT line rate.

