STEP 2 - Leave traffic running (membership maintained, no traffic loss)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u5# ping 239.1.1.1 source 10.10.10.3 repeat 60 interval 1
PING 239.1.1.1 (239.1.1.1) from 10.10.10.3 : 56(84) bytes of data.
--- 239.1.1.1 ping statistics ---
60 packets transmitted, 0 received, 100% packet loss, time 61333ms

host# tcpdump -tni eth2 host 239.1.1.1 and icmp   => 60 frames received of 60 sent (0.0% loss)
   IP 10.10.10.3 > 239.1.1.1: ICMP echo request, id 8892, seq 1, length 64
   IP 10.10.10.3 > 239.1.1.1: ICMP echo request, id 8892, seq 2, length 64
   IP 10.10.10.3 > 239.1.1.1: ICMP echo request, id 8892, seq 3, length 64

u4# show ip igmp groups 239.1.1.1 detail   (maintained across the run)
Group mode:     Exclude (Expires: 00:04:07)
Last reporter:  10.10.10.20
  => 60/60 forwarded, 0% loss.  SCOPE: 60 s / 1 pps sample of the 5-min step, not line rate.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 3 - "Send IGMP leave"   (IGMPv1 protocol note)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
>>> host: IGMPv1 defines NO leave message; membership removed by querier group-timeout

u4# show ip igmp groups
IGMP Connected Group Membership
Group Address    Interface            Uptime   Expires  Last Reporter
239.1.1.1        vlan10               00:01:22 00:04:03 10.10.10.20   <- still present (correct)

u5# ping 239.1.1.1 source 10.10.10.3 repeat 5 interval 1   (after "leave")
--- 239.1.1.1 ping statistics ---
5 packets transmitted, 0 received, 100% packet loss, time 4174ms
host# after leave => 5 frames received (expect 0)
  => CORRECT IGMPv1 BEHAVIOUR: there is no host leave in IGMPv1, so the group persists and
     traffic keeps flowing (5/5 still received). The entry is removed only when the querier's
     group-membership interval (Expires, ~260 s) elapses with no further report. The step-3
     "send leave / group empties" expectation is inherited from the v2/v3 template and does
     not apply to v1. PASS for the protocol.
  NOTE: `show platform table ipmulti` stays at its baseline link entry - same-VLAN L2
  bridged forwarding, no L3 (S,G) mroute (see 38136.log).
